// A field access whose offset the graph cannot prove is a REPORT, not a
// silent trap. The receiver here is a quantified op parameter: the effect
// declares note's argument as the type variable v (lowercase is the
// declaration, SYNTAX's case rule), so the arm binds a universally
// quantified value and there is no record shape to take a slot from.
//
// Before this class existed the compile said NOTHING. The emit wrote
// (unreachable) into the module with a WAT comment naming the field, the
// process exited 0, and the program traps at the instruction that admits
// it. Measured against the pinned boot the day this landed: zero errors,
// 4500 bytes of WAT, one floor inside them.
//
// That is the one promise this boundary exists for, inverted — nothing
// executes unproven. The shipping wheel carried four of these, and the
// march found one the only way a silent floor is ever found: a later
// generation stepped on it and died at a bare wasm trap with no
// diagnostic anywhere in the run.
//
// PRE-ARM CONTRACT (run_narration): the program COMPILES and the class
// surfaces on stderr with no other error beside it. The class arms when
// the wheel's own census of it reaches zero, and on that day this fixture
// moves to run_refusal in the same commit.
effect Col { note(v) -> Int }

handler colh { note(v) => resume(v.zeta), }

fn main() = note({alpha: 7, zeta: 9}) ~> colh
